# Native task accessibility and evidence

Test whether a person can finish the task, understand the result and recover from an interruption. A theme that looks consistent, an automated scan and a written design answer different questions. This page keeps the native and assistive-technology work that is still to do in view, so that an untested task is never reported as a pass.

Other Home Assistant pages link here for how to record their acceptance checks. The examples are local previews with invented values. They do not test or control a home.

## Scope and native ownership

Native dashboard features vary with what each entity can do. Home Assistant owns their focus, keyboard and interaction behaviour. This repository tests the Civica controls it maintains and fixtures shaped like the native source. It does not test a complete Home Assistant installation.

## States and content decisions

| Source condition | Record | Do not |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Source inspected | The file, revision and what it showed | Treat finding it in the source as a tested interaction |
| Automated fixture passed | The fixture, browser, revision and assertions | Extend the pass to other native or custom components |
| Manual task passed | The steps, state, input method and what was observed | Use a screenshot instead of completing the task |
| Not tested or blocked | The missing environment, account, device or method | Turn the absence of a failure into a pass |
| Failure found | The affected task and the conditions that reproduce it | Say a CSS change fixes a backend or semantic fault |

## Integration contract

1. Write one evidence row for each task, state and method. Record the repository revision, the Core and frontend versions, the browser and operating system, the assistive technology and its version, the viewport and zoom, the theme, tone and mode, and the entity capabilities in the fixture.
2. Treat keyboard, screen reader, touch, pointer and voice as separate methods. Test the successful path and also the unavailable, pending, rejected, interrupted and permission-limited outcomes.
3. Keep the native control's meaning. A presentation adapter must preserve the accessible name, role, value, expanded, checked and disabled states, and the link to hints and errors.
4. Keep testing apart from household changes. Use a controlled fixture, or an installation that was agreed to be safe, for any action with consequences. Do not operate a lock or an alarm during an appearance review.

## Accessible interaction

- In a native dialog, check the first focus, that focus stays inside a modal dialog, how Escape and Cancel behave and where focus returns. Check that a nested picker keeps its parent context.
- Test 320px reflow, 200% text and 400% browser zoom as three separate conditions. A small viewport does not show how zoom behaves. Check forced colours and reduced motion separately.
- Screen-reader evidence must say what was announced and whether the person could finish the task. An axe result does not show that.

## Failure and recovery

- Tie a native limitation to the exact version and component. Do not promise that everything is compatible.
- If a control has no alternative to dragging, record the supported route when there is one, and record the task as still failing where there is not.
- If missing equipment blocks a task, record Blocked or Not tested with the missing prerequisite. Do not record a pass.

## Reusable native task matrix

| Task family | Required states and steps | Evidence still needed for a native release |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Slider and volume | Name and value; minimum and maximum; step keys; unavailable and pending | Keyboard and screen reader; touch alternative; 200% text and forced colours |
| Entity and target picker | Search, no results, unavailable match, selected count, permission scope | Keyboard order; selection announcement; long names; how fresh the native data is |
| Nested automation editor | Add, reorder, expand, validate, undo; save kept apart from run | A route without dragging; hierarchy; screen-reader editing; the draft kept after a rejection |
| Camera and media | Loading, missing stream, paused or live; labelled controls over imagery | Keyboard and screen reader; captions where the content needs them; no autoplay |
| Map and zone editor | A text route to the location, grouped markers, missing coordinates, zoom and exit | A route to editing without dragging; attribution; keyboard traps and shared-screen privacy |
| Native more-info dialog | Open, nested control, error, close, focus return | Dialog context in a screen reader; Escape; enlarged text; the outcome of the native action |
| Dense or shared display | Long names, many entities, changing counts and private records | 320px, 200% text, 400% zoom, forced colours, reduced motion and the chosen level of disclosure |

## Executed evidence and its limits

The [published guidance/audit run at revision fc393e4](https://github.com/nathcymru/HA-Theme-gov.uk/actions/runs/43103696048) passed 531 browser checks for the then-current build. Its record covers 165 guides and 301 examples, including documentation accessibility/reflow, safe local example behaviour and the maintained runtime fixtures. These are historical results, not fresh passes for this expanded page set. The [work-package record](../reference/guidance-work-package.json) retains that scope.

| Executed test family | What its evidence covers | What it does not show |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Documentation browser checks | The built markup, automated accessibility, narrow layouts, content without JavaScript and local example behaviour | Screen-reader use or native device tasks |
| Theme settings and badge fixtures | Palette, tone and mode; named controls; count updates; duplicate loading and restoring | Every native profile or sidebar version, or notification delivery |
| Lighting and legacy-card fixtures | Named controls, unavailable and error states, dialog and scene presentation and cleanup | A physical light or appliance working |
| Energy real-renderer fixtures | Native-shaped ECharts data, table values, signed traces, locale, patterns and restoring | A full Home Assistant installation, every chart type or a screen-reader task study |

The [v1.3.2 verification record](https://github.com/nathcymru/HA-Theme-gov.uk/blob/fc393e49205926b753d1c531358c5e627c9c2af6/VERIFICATION.md) separately records 50 Node checks, 52 browser checks and 37 documentation pages for that earlier runtime correction. Do not add those historical counts together or relabel them as current coverage. Live palette/chart observations recorded in release evidence do not cover physical device execution or all native task rows above. Human screen-reader, household-comprehension and complete live-task coverage remain separate acceptance work.

